---
layout: base.njk
title: Close CRM integration
description: "Prospektor finds the companies worth approaching and writes the pitch. One press files it in Close as a lead, its contacts, an opportunity and a note."
# One page per language (#114/#535, the same shape the funnel and the two
# product pages take) — see src/index.njk for the reasoning.
pagination:
  data: languages
  size: 1
  alias: language
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "{{ language.prefix }}/integrations/close/"
---

{#- #620, 10 Sep 2026; rewritten by #830 and reshaped by #838, 28 Sep 2026.
    The page Close's integration directory points at
    (close.com/integrations/prospektor) and the answer to two required fields
    on their listing form (#9 Marketing URL, and "do you promote Close on your
    website in any way?").

    THE SHAPE is Close's own integration page (close.com/integrations/addtocrm),
    at the operator's ask (#838): "It should look something like this and not
    a long AI-written page. More visual, less text, clear CTA." So: a back
    link and the mark, a sidebar that holds the one action and the support
    links, two visuals, about a hundred words and three numbered steps, the
    buy card, and the other integrations under it. #830's ask still binds
    every sentence: humanized, the free month on every screen, and no census
    of the other tools on Close's shelf.

    THE ONE THING THIS PAGE MUST NOT DO: sell whom to chase. Its visitor
    already has a CRM and already believes in it. Everything here is the half
    Close does not have, and where it lands when it is done.

    `/integrations/` rather than `/partners/` (which implies a programme the
    product does not have and would collide with the unbuilt affiliate scheme,
    #87) and rather than `/close/` (a common English word that tells a visitor
    nothing). It mirrors Close's own `close.com/integrations/<name>`, so it
    reads as native from their directory, and since #838 it is the directory
    `/integrations/` sits over.

    Every claim here is the studio's code, read on 28 Sep 2026, and if one of
    them stops being true this page is wrong, not modest:
      - the one-press connect is the Close OAuth app (#582/#583, live since
        `6aa20f8` on the studio), so no key is pasted;
      - what a push writes is `lib/crm-close.js` (#582, proven in production
        by the operator's own press on 10 Sep): the lead found by domain, its
        contacts, an opportunity whose CONFIDENCE is the fit score, and a
        note that renders; a second press updates by id.
    The first visual is drawn here, in the site's tokens, and names those
    four records and nothing else; the second is a real screen off the demo's
    capture (#767), the fit thesis that becomes the note.

    THE OFFER IS WRITTEN ONLY WHEN THIS BUILD ARMS IT (#622). Every sentence
    that says "free", "30 days" or "$0" sits inside `{% if offer.close %}`, so
    the page cannot promise a month the checkout call would not grant, and the
    dark build is the same page at list price. `test/close.test.js` builds
    both and reads every "N days" against `lib/trial.js`. -#}

<section class="int-page">
  <a class="int-back" href="{{ '/integrations/' | localize }}">{% t %}← All integrations{% endt %}</a>
  <div class="int-head">
    <span class="int-mark" aria-hidden="true">Cs</span>
    <div>
      <h1>Close</h1>
      <p class="int-sub">{% t %}Prospektor writes the pitch. Close works the deal.{% endt %}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="int-body">
    <aside class="int-side">
      {%- if offer.close %}
      <a class="btn-cta" href="#start">{% t %}Start my free month →{% endt %}</a>
      <p class="int-side-offer">{% t %}<strong>One month free for Close users.</strong> Card on file, nothing charged for 30 days, and one email cancels.{% endt %}</p>
      {%- else %}
      <a class="btn-cta" href="#start">{% t %}Start my studio →{% endt %}</a>
      {%- endif %}
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="mailto:hello@prospektor.ai">{% t %}Integration support{% endt %}</a>
      <ul class="int-links">
        <li><a href="{{ '/help/workspace/' | localize }}#workspace--crm-a-finished-pitch-pushed-into-hubspot-affinity-close-or-lightfield">{% t %}Documentation{% endt %}</a></li>
        <li><a href="{{ '/terms/' | localize }}">{% t %}Terms of service{% endt %}</a></li>
        <li><a href="{{ '/privacy/' | localize }}">{% t %}Privacy policy{% endt %}</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="int-built">{% t %}Built by Prospektor{% endt %}</p>
    </aside>

    <div class="int-main">
      {#- Visual 1: what one press writes into Close, drawn in the site's own
          tokens. Four rows, one per record lib/crm-close.js writes, and the
          press that writes them. Text as text, so it reads in every language
          and to a screen reader. -#}
      <figure class="int-visual">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 720 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="intPushTitle" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <title id="intPushTitle">{% t %}One press in Prospektor writes four records in Close{% endt %}</title>
          <rect width="720" height="300" style="fill:var(--off-white)"/>
          <!-- the pitch, on the left -->
          <rect x="34" y="60" width="200" height="180" rx="14" style="fill:var(--white);stroke:var(--border)"/>
          <text x="54" y="92" style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;fill:var(--accent-dim);letter-spacing:.06em">PROSPEKTOR</text>
          <text x="54" y="122" style="font-family:var(--font);font-size:17px;font-weight:800;fill:var(--ink)">Harborline Freight</text>
          <rect x="54" y="140" width="120" height="8" rx="4" style="fill:var(--stone)"/>
          <rect x="54" y="156" width="150" height="8" rx="4" style="fill:var(--stone)"/>
          <rect x="54" y="172" width="96" height="8" rx="4" style="fill:var(--stone)"/>
          <rect x="54" y="198" width="118" height="28" rx="14" style="fill:var(--coral)"/>
          <text x="113" y="216" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:var(--font);font-size:12px;font-weight:700;fill:#fff">{% t %}Push to Close{% endt %}</text>
          <!-- the arrow -->
          <path d="M248 150 H298" style="stroke:var(--ink-faint);stroke-width:2;fill:none"/>
          <path d="M292 143 L300 150 L292 157" style="stroke:var(--ink-faint);stroke-width:2;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/>
          <!-- the lead in Close, on the right -->
          <rect x="316" y="30" width="370" height="240" rx="14" style="fill:var(--white);stroke:var(--border)"/>
          <text x="338" y="60" style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;fill:var(--ink-faint);letter-spacing:.06em">CLOSE</text>
          <g style="font-family:var(--font);font-size:13px">
            <rect x="338" y="78" width="326" height="1" style="fill:var(--border)"/>
            <text x="338" y="106" style="font-weight:800;fill:var(--ink)">{% t %}Lead{% endt %}</text>
            <text x="440" y="106" style="fill:var(--ink-mid)">{% t %}matched on its web domain{% endt %}</text>
            <rect x="338" y="122" width="326" height="1" style="fill:var(--border)"/>
            <text x="338" y="150" style="font-weight:800;fill:var(--ink)">{% t %}Contacts{% endt %}</text>
            <text x="440" y="150" style="fill:var(--ink-mid)">{% t %}the decision-makers, with sources{% endt %}</text>
            <rect x="338" y="166" width="326" height="1" style="fill:var(--border)"/>
            <text x="338" y="194" style="font-weight:800;fill:var(--ink)">{% t %}Opportunity{% endt %}</text>
            <text x="440" y="194" style="fill:var(--ink-mid)">{% t %}confidence = the fit score{% endt %}</text>
            <rect x="338" y="210" width="326" height="1" style="fill:var(--border)"/>
            <text x="338" y="238" style="font-weight:800;fill:var(--ink)">{% t %}Note{% endt %}</text>
            <text x="440" y="238" style="fill:var(--ink-mid)">{% t %}the fit, the angle, the sources, a link back{% endt %}</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>{% t %}One press, four records. Push again and the same four update.{% endt %}</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="int-visual">
        <img src="{{ '/assets/img/demo/step-03.png' | asset }}" width="1280" height="800" loading="lazy"
             alt="{% t %}A finished pitch in Prospektor: the fit thesis, with the case for the company, the case against it, and what they will say.{% endt %}">
        <figcaption>{% t %}The fit thesis in Prospektor, which is what the note in Close holds.{% endt %}</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="int-text">
        <p>
          {% t %}Prospektor finds the companies worth approaching, names who to talk to
          and writes what you send them, in your voice. One press files all of it in
          Close, where your team already works.{% endt %}
        </p>
        <p>
          {% t %}Four records, the way Close models a deal: the <strong>lead</strong>,
          matched on its web domain, its <strong>contacts</strong>, an
          <strong>opportunity</strong> with the fit score as its confidence, and a
          <strong>note</strong>.{% endt %}
        </p>
        <p>
          {% t %}The note holds the fit, the angle, the sources and a link back to the
          full pitch. Push again and the same records update; nothing is created
          twice.{% endt %}
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>{% t %}Press <strong>Connect Close</strong> in your workspace settings and approve it on Close's screen. There is no API key.{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Run a pitch on a company you want.{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Press <strong>Push to Close</strong>.{% endt %}</li>
        </ol>
        {%- if offer.close %}
        <p>
          {% t %}<strong>One month free for Close users.</strong> Card on file, nothing charged
          for 30 days, and one email to
          <a href="mailto:hello@prospektor.ai">hello@prospektor.ai</a> cancels.{% endt %}
        </p>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="pricing pricing-page" id="start">
    <div class="pricing-card">
      {#- Monthly only, deliberately: the offer below is a free month converting to
          a monthly subscription, and a plan switch beside it would be a second
          decision on a page that already has one (the style skill, rule 8). The
          yearly plan is one click away on /pricing/. -#}
      <div class="price-row">
        <span class="price-num">$999</span>
        <span class="price-per">{% t %}/ month · per workspace{% endt %}</span>
      </div>

      {%- if offer.close %}
      {#- #622. Written ONLY when this build's environment arms the offer, so the
          page cannot advertise a trial the checkout call would not grant — and
          the number below is `lib/trial.js`'s constant, which is also the only
          value `CLOSE_TRIAL_DAYS` will accept. test/close.test.js pins the two
          together in both directions. -#}
      <div class="onboard-note">
        <p>{% t %}<strong>First month free for Close users.</strong> Card on file, nothing
          charged for 30 days. Cancel inside them with one email to
          <a href="mailto:hello@prospektor.ai">hello@prospektor.ai</a> and you are
          never charged.{% endt %}</p>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}

      <ul class="pricing-list">
        <li>{% t %}Unlimited pitch runs: research, scoring and every deliverable{% endt %}</li>
        <li>{% t %}Up to 100 companies in one batch, drafted while the tab is closed{% endt %}</li>
        <li>{% t %}Every colleague on your work-email domain, at no extra cost{% endt %}</li>
        <li>{% t %}Every finished pitch pushed to Close with one press{% endt %}</li>
      </ul>

      {#- The same markup, ids and script as /pricing/'s tile: one field, then
          Stripe. `data-via` is what makes this arrival the Close one — it is on
          the FORM rather than read from the URL, so the offer belongs to the page
          that states it and no query parameter a stranger types can claim it.
          `data-from` sends a cancelled checkout back here instead of to /#pricing. -#}
      <div class="buy" id="buy">
        {%- if offer.close %}
        <a href="{{ '/checkout/' | localize }}" class="btn-cta" id="buyLink">{% t %}Start my free month →{% endt %}</a>
        {%- else %}
        <a href="{{ '/checkout/' | localize }}" class="btn-cta" id="buyLink">{% t %}Start my studio →{% endt %}</a>
        {%- endif %}
        <form class="reserve-form buy-form" id="buyForm" data-via="close" data-from="close" hidden novalidate>
          <input class="reserve-input" id="buyEmail" type="email" autocomplete="email"
                 placeholder="you@yourcompany.com" aria-label="{% t %}Your work email{% endt %}">
          <button class="btn-cta" type="submit" id="buyBtn">
            {%- if offer.close %}{% t %}Start my free month · $0 today →{% endt %}{% else %}{% t %}Pay &amp; start · $999/mo →{% endt %}{% endif -%}
          </button>
        </form>
        <input class="reserve-input buy-site" id="buySite" type="text" inputmode="url" autocomplete="url"
               placeholder="yourcompany.com" aria-label="{% t %}Your company website{% endt %}" hidden>
        <p class="reserve-msg is-error" id="buyMsg" hidden></p>
        <p class="buy-note">
          <span id="buyLive" hidden>{% t %}Next stop is Stripe. This address becomes your studio's sign-in, and a work email brings your whole team in with you.{% endt %} </span>
          {%- if offer.close %}{% t %}Nothing is charged for 30 days. After that, money back any month it doesn't earn its keep.{% endt %}{% else %}{% t %}Money back if it doesn't earn its keep, with no fourteen days of hoping you remember to cancel.{% endt %}{% endif %}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</section>
{#- defer, like every script this site serves (#137/#170). buy.js looks its
    elements up by id and returns if they are absent, so this page and
    /pricing/ share it without either knowing about the other. No plan.js:
    there is no switch on this page to drive. -#}
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/buy.js' | asset }}" defer></script>

<section class="int-more">
  <h2 class="sec-mid">{% t %}More integrations from Prospektor{% endt %}</h2>
  {% set skipApp = 'close' %}
  {% include "integrations-grid.njk" %}
  <p class="int-more-all"><a class="btn-ghost" href="{{ '/integrations/' | localize }}">{% t %}See all integrations →{% endt %}</a></p>
</section>
